      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-63619",
      ":question/problem": "Monthly, Luz's salary is always $$100$ more than Nelson's salary.\n\nIf $l$ represents Luz's salary and $n$ represents Nelson's salary, then which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $n = l + 100$\n2. $l$ is the dependent variable\n3. $n$ is the independent variable"
